# Working notes stay private. These carry the reasoning, the defects found,
# the checksums and the open items, and are not written for a reader.
*_Findings.md
*_findings.md
*Findings*.md
*_Conformance*.md
*_Retrieval*.md
*_Update*.md
*Notes.md

# Preserved sources and pass baselines. Never published, never overwritten.
RECEIVED_*
RECEIVED__*
PRESPEC_*
PRE_UPDATE__*
SOURCE_*
SOURCE__*
INBOUND_*
*.frozen
*.keep
sources/
SOURCE_ARCHIVE/
_source_snapshots/

# The .received-<date>. infix convention, caught by name rather than by
# location, so a snapshot dropped outside _source_snapshots/ is still excluded.
*.received-*
*.received-*.md

# Scripts a pass writes for itself, and their output.
check_*.py
diff_*.py
probe_*.py
apply_*.py
*.log
CHECKSUMS.txt

# The governing document and its templates are the working reference,
# not part of the published set. Remove these two lines if you want them public.
HOUSE_STYLE.md
TEMPLATE_*.html

# Snapshots of the governing document. The text is excluded for the same reason
# HOUSE_STYLE.md itself is, two rules above: it is the working reference and not
# part of the published set, and a tracked copy would defeat that exclusion. The
# hash-only record in SPEC_VERSIONS.md is tracked instead, which is what lets a
# later pass detect that the specification moved without publishing its prose.
spec_snapshots/

# Local tooling config, not project content.
.claude/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Verification harness, the baseline directories it works against, and scratch
# working material. All are working apparatus, not published research: the
# harness encodes the checks and their repairs, preserved/ and preserve/ hold
# each pass's source as it stood before its first edit under the older and the
# current naming respectively, and scratch/ holds spec-derived working material
# for passes in progress. Kept in the project so they survive a temp-directory
# clearance, and excluded here so they never reach the published set.
harness/
preserved/
preserve/
scratch/
*.ps1
_preserved*/
received*/
as_received/

# Pass documentation. Every findings, results, conformance, update, register and
# build document a pass writes about its own work, gathered in one folder so the
# main folder holds the deliverables and the little the site needs.
#
# The name rules at the top of this file already catch these one at a time, but
# they catch them by name and only because this checkout matches ignore patterns
# without regard to case: FINDINGS_2026-08-05_HUT_Correction_Pass.md meets
# *Findings*.md here and would not on a case-sensitive checkout. Binding the
# folder excludes a document by where it was written rather than by what it
# happened to be called, so a note named nothing in particular is still excluded.
pass_documentation/
